  "id": "subject-matching",
  "term": "subject matching",
  "definition": "Subject matching is the process of aligning one person’s brain images with those of other people or with a common template so the images can be compared in the same space. In this source, it refers especially to direct matching of one subject’s EPI scans across subjects rather than relying on a separate anatomical image to guide the alignment.",
